v0.10.29: publish-checks UX — case-sensitivity bug + actionable checklist

Mario clicked Publish on efra_ai_01_scout and saw literally
"Cannot publish:" in the toast pill — no reasons, no guidance.
Screenshot showed all three required fields empty (description,
system_prompt, tags) but the toast rendered as if there were no
failing checks.

Root cause: case-sensitivity bug in the frontend filter.

  Rust side (src/workflows/types.rs):
    #[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]
    #[serde(rename_all = "lowercase")]
    pub enum CheckSeverity { Error, Warning, Info }

  → JSON emits severity as "error" / "warning" / "info".

  Frontend filter (three sites):
    checks.filter(c => !c.passed && c.severity === "Error")
                                              ↑ capitalized, matches NOTHING

  → `failing` always empty → toast renders "Cannot publish: " with
  no content after.

The App-creation path in xaman-ek.js had the right filter
(severity === "error") from day one. Only the agent-publish flow
had the typo. Every "Cannot publish" pill on this platform has
been misleading since the code shipped — silent because the
codepath wasn't reachable end-to-end until v0.10.15 (admin bypass)
and v0.10.27 (agents.updated_at) opened it up.

Change (three sites, all one-liner case fixes):

  templates/agent_detail.html::publishAgent
    * severity === "Error" → "error"
    * Toast.show(...) → alert(...) so the checklist is legible on
      narrow viewports (Toast has no max-width guard)
    * Formatted as bulleted list + "how to fix" hint

  templates/agent_detail.html::adminPublishAgentDetail
    * severity === "Error" → "error"
    * (existing alert format preserved)

  templates/admin.html::adminPublishAgent
    * severity === "Error" → "error"
    * (existing alert format preserved)

Mario now sees:

  Cannot publish yet — fix the following before retrying:

    • Description is required for publication
    • System prompt is required for publication
    • At least one tag is required

  Edit these fields in the Manage tab, then click Publish again.

(v0.10.28 was Ivan's parallel fermi-console charts release,
unrelated to this hotfix.)

Not in scope:
  - Persistent publish-readiness checklist on the Manage tab
    (live-updating as-you-type). Nicer UX than modal-on-click;
    v0.10.30 candidate.
  - Admin bulk view "agents that would fail publish checks"
    dashboard. Mario has clear per-agent feedback now; bulk view
    can wait.

Sixth "platform assumed X but shipped Y" bug in the run since
v0.10.15. The v0.11.0 trust-contract now needs BOTH DB-schema-
drift and wire-format-drift checks — a Rust↔JSON case-consistency
sweep (all serde rename_all values documented + JS/TS shape tests)
would have caught this at CI.

Related:
  v0.10.15   admin force-publish (introduced the bug in admin flows)
  v0.10.27   agents.updated_at unblocked the codepath end-to-end
  v0.10.28   Ivan's parallel charts release (unrelated)
  v0.10.30   candidate: persistent readiness checklist + admin bulk view
  v0.11.0    trust-contract, now covering wire-format drift too
